Scripts to produce Baobab Ntuples
---------------------------------

Author: Ph. Gras. CEA/Saclay


Usage:
-----

1. Set crab 3 environment
2. Set up Tuple enviroment following instructions from https://github.com/UGent/Tupel/blob/Tupel_MiniAOD/Tupel/readme.txt.
3. Run grow_baobabs. See options in the next section.

Important: CMSSW environment must be set after the crab 3 environment. Otherwise you will inherit from a Python version too old for the Baobab production tools.

Different options of grow_baobabs run:
------------------------------------

To submit new jobs, you should specify the catalog of dataset to process [1], like this:

./grow_baobabs.py datasets.txt

To check running job and generate lumi section summary json file, use the --check option:

./grow_baobabs.py --check

The production is kept track in the baobab_prod.sqlite3 database file. For a production, it is important to run grow_baobabs.py always in the same disk directory as this database file is picked up form the working directory.

To list the content of the production database file, used the --list option:

./grow_baobabs.py --list

simple_grow_baobabs
-------------------

simple_grow_baobabs is a simple script to submit the jobs to produce Baobab ntuples. It does not keep track of the production as grow_baobabs does. For a central production, grow_baobabs should be used


[1] https://twiki.cern.ch/twiki/bin/view/CMS/SmpVjBaobabProduction
